{
 "id": "auth",
 "question": "How do I authenticate and get an API key?",
 "voice": "meher",
 "model": "lightning_v3.1_pro",
 "sample_rate": 24000,
 "durationSec": 34.379125,
 "narration": "Create your key on the API Keys page. One key covers models and voice agents. Keep it on the server and send it as Authorization Bearer. The browser requests a short lived token from your server. The server calls /console/v1/auth/token and sets ttl_seconds between 30 and 900. Hey Smallest asks for 300 seconds. The access token starts with wat. Browsers pass it as api_key on the WebSocket. Tokens may call TTS and STT. Electron and voice cloning return 403 to a token, so those stay on the server.",
